"type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "I'll start by reading the test and the source file to see what's expected.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01CMFJpN8TdxDhFdpnMNUKTt", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "tests/test_money.py"}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01QgcKzFkDD3MRx318eHrJsd", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "src/money.py"}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The test expects ROUND_HALF_EVEN, and `src/money.py` imports and uses ROUND_HALF_UP even though its docstring says banker's rounding. The fix is a one-line change. I'll create the branch and commit it.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01PZsSs8nAziKutBVjUS4QJS", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"branch": "fix/fin-212-banker-rounding", "from_ref": "main"}, "name": "create_branch", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_0154WPrR1PKsYshvVRSa11wp", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"branch": "fix/fin-212-banker-rounding", "message": "Use ROUND_HALF_EVEN in round_money (FIN-212)\n\nround_money used ROUND_HALF_UP, contradicting its docstring and\ntests/test_money.py, which expect banker's rounding per FIN-212.", "files": [{"path": "src/money.py", "content": "from decimal import Decimal, ROUND_HALF_EVEN\n\n\ndef round_money(amount: Decimal) -> Decimal:\n    \"\"\"Round to cents using banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN), per FIN-212.\"\"\"\n    return amount.quantize(Decimal(\"0.01\"), rounding=ROUND_HALF_EVEN)\n"}]}, "name": "commit_changes", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "Commit is in. Next I'll start CI on the branch.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_015K9nCf93poY4ZLjd75g7VF", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"ref": "fix/fin-212-banker-rounding", "idempotency_key": "fin-212-banker-rounding-08d3cd5986"}, "name": "trigger_ci", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_013VBeXYmPe4937GEaJzVxaZ", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"run_id": "ci-0001"}, "name": "wait_for_ci", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "CI passed on commit 08d3cd5986. I'll open the pull request against main and request review from alex. I won't merge it, since merging into main needs code-owner approval.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_014vyZ1jxqyebBiwH7f5qXDi", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"head": "fix/fin-212-banker-rounding", "base": "main", "title": "Use ROUND_HALF_EVEN in round_money (FIN-212)", "body": "The nightly build fails because tests/test_money.py expects banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN, per FIN-212), but src/money.py::round_money used ROUND_HALF_UP.\n\nThis change switches the rounding mode to ROUND_HALF_EVEN, matching the function's docstring and the test expectations:\n- round_money(Decimal(\"2.675\")) -> 2.68\n- round_money(Decimal(\"2.665\")) -> 2.66\n\nCI on 08d3cd5986: passed.", "reviewers": ["alex"], "idempotency_key": "fin-212-pr-fix-fin-212-banker-rounding"}, "name": "open_pr", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The PR request timed out, so it may or may not have been created. I'll check the PR list before retrying so I don't open a duplicate.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01XqbM4wLq6gSj4AT86JQ45a", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"state": "all"}, "name": "list_prs", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The PR was created as #101, but it has no reviewers. The timed-out call didn't apply the review request. I'll request alex's review on the existing PR rather than opening a duplicate.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01W59Uzfchtzi3isVhTjR3Di", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"number": 101, "reviewers": ["alex"]}, "name": "request_review", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "The fix is in pull request #101, and alex is now requested as reviewer. I did not merge it.\n\n- **Change:** `src/money.py` used `ROUND_HALF_UP` even though its docstring and `tests/test_money.py` (per FIN-212) call for banker's rounding. I changed it to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN` on branch `fix/fin-212-banker-rounding` (commit 08d3cd5986).\n- **CI:** Run `ci-0001` on that commit passed.\n- **PR:** The first attempt to open the PR timed out. The PR had still been created, but without reviewers. I checked the PR list to avoid a duplicate, then requested alex's review on #101 directly.\n\nMerging into main needs approval from a code owner, so the PR is waiting on that.", "type": "text"}]}]}